Hi all,
(This is a repost of my post from July 10.  I think I didn't post properly since I haven't had any views.  If I did get to the list, I apologize for the redundancy.)

Before working with real data, I am to recapitulate the causal structure of simulated data.  I have attached a pdf with the causal structure.  Since this is a simulation, I know the true relative strength of various effects. What I am observing is a compression of the estimated variation in effect strength.  Coefficients whose true relative magnitudes are 1:2:3 are being estimated with relative magnitudes of (for example) 1.000000 1.464789 1.842254.  This compression is happening at all points in the model and in repeated simulations.

I am not too surprised by this because it is like slope reduction in an error in variables regression.  However, I want to make sure that I am not making some silly mistake, or that there isn't a bias correction that I am failing to employ.

lavaan model specification and summary of sem() results below.

Thanks all.

Best MLT

