I brought this to your attention a couple of weeks ago (direct email) and you said I needed to use =~ operator or LAVAAN wouldn't know the variables are latent.  OK, but the documentation indicates that  =~ operator is an effect indicator operator which means "is manifested by" .  What I need to communicate to LAVAAN is a causal indicator relationship "is caused by".  To avoid running the causal arrows in the wrong direction, I tried the syntax we both think looks odd.  It runs without an error statement and gives reasonable results except for the flattening of effects that I mentioned (which may actually be reasonable).

